================================================================================
## Route AI Gateway models correctly when proposing hypothetical facts
================================================================================

Context: On the deployed app, Propose facts returned "Could not propose
hypothetical facts". App logs showed a 404 ENDPOINT_NOT_FOUND against
``/serving-endpoints/databricks-claude-opus-4-6/invocations``. That name is an
AI Gateway Foundation Model, not a serving endpoint. The domain picker stores
``llm_endpoint_kind=ai_gateway``, but the simulation-facts (and Graph Chat)
agents dropped the kind and inferred serving from the name. Production also
strips error detail, so the UI hid the 404.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_simulation_facts/engine.py
   Accept ``endpoint_kind`` and pass it to ``call_serving_endpoint``.
2. src/api/routers/internal/simulation.py
   Forward the domain LLM kind; map missing-endpoint failures to a client-safe
   message (detail is stripped in production).
3. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
   Same ``endpoint_kind`` pass-through so Graph Chat uses the Gateway URL.
4. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   Forward the domain LLM kind on Graph Chat and Graph Chat stream.
5. tests/units/agents/test_agent_simulation_facts.py
   Assert the facts agent forwards ``endpoint_kind=ai_gateway``.
6. tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_runner_api.py
   Assert the route forwards kind and names a missing Gateway model.
7. tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat_engine.py
   Assert Graph Chat forwards ``endpoint_kind``.

