## List Results triples when the before-picture companion is missing
================================================================================

Context: The Results tab painted KPIs from the stored ``diff_summary`` but the
Added/Removed table showed "Nothing here." ``GET /simulation/{id}/diff`` treated
a missing ``__smb_`` companion as empty rows and still returned the last-run
counts. Older runs never created that companion; probing it with
``query_triples`` also hid a present empty table behind a full scan. Persist
the before-picture with an in-database clone, and fall back to stored diff
rows for scenarios that have not been re-run.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/SimulationStore.py
   ``clone_sandbox_table`` copies ``__sim_`` into ``__smb_`` with INSERT…SELECT.
2. src/back/objects/simulation/Sandbox.py
   ``persist_before`` uses the SQL clone when the store supports it; existence
   uses ``table_exists`` instead of loading every triple.
3. src/back/objects/simulation/Simulation.py
   If the companion is missing, page stored ``diff`` rows when present; otherwise
   flag ``listing_unavailable`` instead of pairing KPIs with an empty table.
4. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-results.js
   Empty-state copy tells the user to re-run when the listing is unavailable.
5. tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_core.py
   Cover SQL clone, persist-before clone, and ``table_exists`` probe.
6. tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_runner_api.py
   Cover stored-row fallback and the unavailable-listing flag.
7. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
   Require the re-run empty-state copy.

